{"id": "EUVD-2026-86777", "enisaUuid": "d9956f32-9ef6-37b1-aa8a-5be9d32234cc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing: Free histogram the var ref when its initialization fails\n\ncreate_var_ref() allocates a VAR_REF hist_field and then calls\ninit_var_ref() to fill it in. When that fails the field is leaked.\n\ncommit 656fe2ba85e8 (\"tracing: Use hist trigger's var_ref array to destroy\nvar_refs\") made destroy_hist_field() return early for\nHIST_FIELD_FL_VAR_REF, since var refs are freed by walking the trigger's\nvar_refs[] array instead. create_var_ref() adds the field to that array\nonly after init_var_ref() has succeeded, so on this path the field is in\nneither place and nothing frees it. The call was correct when it was\nwritten, before var refs were taken out of destroy_hist_field().\n\ninit_var_ref() cannot free it either. The caller owns the field, so\ninit_var_ref() undoes only its own string allocations and leaves the\nfield alone. Freeing it there would leave create_var_ref() passing freed\nmemory to destroy_hist_field(), which reads its flags.\n\nCall __destroy_hist_field(), which frees the field without consulting\nthe flag.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:50", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/608b7751926ec08fae6a1ac4e7308195da68c362", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4870f9071c9ea3c1423a07741b85a794db30d672", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/352f84a381e7b4651b30366e93cb858f3fa9c91a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4924328d6991f25b65bb7c8ff5d56c2a9b254851", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/74375caa20fe5165807b4334c783d1790b01f02a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/222abcbe7866fef04563b6eb89fb21f627dcbc77", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a69baeac38677270656e85753d93856a076dee57", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/516001d53e6b2ea95a251ee2ef54a1a689a3fd58"], "aliases": ["GHSA-28hv-8h97-8cx6", "CVE-2026-97923"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "121516f5-b0ca-38fa-be47-bd6e3ba0775a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "280ae5dc-c8e7-3040-81f5-0aa125950691", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.19.100 <4.20"}, {"id": "2a57afd3-bf3f-3d32-b728-f2b1d7389449", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "656fe2ba85e81d00e4447bf77b8da2be3c47acb2 <516001d53e6b2ea95a251ee2ef54a1a689a3fd58"}, {"id": "312eaf56-3911-34b1-9c1d-299703c22393", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "836717841a30d7845cdf9cb806ee0ff3bfa7135a"}, {"id": "45c86cb6-dd0e-35a9-8871-693b2734b780", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "4d9b8039-adf0-33e3-a654-be9e15d47846", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "656fe2ba85e81d00e4447bf77b8da2be3c47acb2 <352f84a381e7b4651b30366e93cb858f3fa9c91a"}, {"id": "60ee336a-1527-3a52-aa5b-f4628b040747", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "656fe2ba85e81d00e4447bf77b8da2be3c47acb2 <74375caa20fe5165807b4334c783d1790b01f02a"}, {"id": "68e4fe7a-89d1-3040-a285-f24701e50f5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6f7a6d14-2b6a-3360-a487-dea60c4ce22e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "8b6bc3c0-5883-3929-a449-981f6812a25d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "976cd92b-31ec-33c7-9a01-f8de29565afc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.0"}, {"id": "9e580161-d89e-32fd-8e5a-db08d3e7f60c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "656fe2ba85e81d00e4447bf77b8da2be3